column7:
From May 15 to 19, 2024, the DORS/CLUC conference was held, with the full name Days of Open Computer Systems / Croatian Linux Users' Conference. 
The conference was organized by two associations (HrOpen and HULK), with the support and partnership of FER, and is dedicated to developer and system - administrator topics, with a focus on free and open technologies, open code, open norms and open operating systems.
For the first time, it will also include State of the Map Croatia - the first official OpenStreetMap event in Croatia.
The conference ended on May 18 and 19, 2024 with the Zagreb Unikraft Hackathon.   
Keynote speakers were: 
Laura Durieux, multiple award-winning developer; 
Ievgen Pyrogov, devops engineer with more than 15 years of experience; 
Ivan Voras, doctor of computer science, was one of the main developers of the FreeBSD operating system, entrepreneur and experienced CTO, who has been promoting open technologies for over 25 years;
Davor Virag, doctor of medicine and scientist who uses open technologies in his research.
